# Remember to never publicly share your keystore.
# See https://flutter.dev/to/reference-keystore
key.properties
**/*.keystore
**/*.jks

# Those three rules are load-bearing, not boilerplate. DraconDex signs its
# release APK with a PRIVATE keystore held in repo secrets
# (ANDROID_KEYSTORE_BASE64 and friends, decoded into android/app/release.keystore
# by .github/workflows/build-apk.yml at build time), so a key.properties or
# keystore appearing in a working tree is someone's local copy and must never be
# committed. See docs/UPDATE.md sections 2.11 and 2.13.
#
# build-apk.yml does also accept a keystore committed to the repo as a fallback
# — that is how ZYDRAXYL/QuetzaLib-APP does it, and it needs no secrets at all.
# Taking that route means deliberately re-including the two files here:
#
#     !key.properties
#     !app/release.keystore
#
# Do not add those lines casually. They make the signing identity PUBLIC:
# anyone who can read the repo could then build an APK that Android accepts as
# an update over an existing DraconDex install. Switching between the two
# routes also breaks in-app updates for everyone already installed, exactly as
# losing the keystore does.
